1
00:00:00,800 --> 00:00:03,531
An agent that remembers everything has a problem.

2
00:00:03,531 --> 00:00:05,580
It cannot tell you what changed.

3
00:00:06,180 --> 00:00:07,624
A README says Redis.

4
00:00:07,624 --> 00:00:09,429
A Slack thread proposes Postgres.

5
00:00:09,429 --> 00:00:11,234
A pull request implements it.

6
00:00:11,234 --> 00:00:12,678
A runbook confirms it.

7
00:00:12,678 --> 00:00:14,844
All four are still in memory.

8
00:00:14,844 --> 00:00:18,815
Ask where session state lives now, and a retriever hands the

9
00:00:18,815 --> 00:00:20,620
model all four and hopes.

10
00:00:21,220 --> 00:00:23,933
Lacuna is a context layer built on HydraDB.

11
00:00:23,933 --> 00:00:27,663
It reads the conversations, turns them into claims that carry a

12
00:00:27,663 --> 00:00:31,393
time and a source, and answers from the claims rather than

13
00:00:31,393 --> 00:00:32,410
from the text.

14
00:00:33,010 --> 00:00:34,413
Prose becomes claims here.

15
00:00:34,413 --> 00:00:37,569
A suggestion files where the resolver cannot read it.

16
00:00:37,569 --> 00:00:41,076
So does a line ordering the system to record something.

17
00:00:41,076 --> 00:00:43,180
Neither one can become an answer.

18
00:00:43,780 --> 00:00:47,393
This is the deployed product, and every row on it is

19
00:00:47,393 --> 00:00:49,035
computed when the page loads.

20
00:00:49,035 --> 00:00:52,320
Current state: answered, with the two sources it rests on.

21
00:00:52,920 --> 00:00:54,273
A value that changed.

22
00:00:54,273 --> 00:00:56,302
The answer is the current one.

23
00:00:56,302 --> 00:01:00,022
The one it replaced stays readable as history, because nothing is

24
00:01:00,022 --> 00:01:02,390
deleted to make the picture look clean.

25
00:01:02,990 --> 00:01:04,165
Two sources disagree.

26
00:01:04,165 --> 00:01:06,907
Lacuna keeps both and refuses to pick.

27
00:01:06,907 --> 00:01:11,217
A confident guess here is the failure this whole product exists

28
00:01:11,217 --> 00:01:12,000
to prevent.

29
00:01:12,600 --> 00:01:15,626
A real subject, and a value nobody ever stated.

30
00:01:15,626 --> 00:01:19,324
No evidence, so no answer, and the reason is on the

31
00:01:19,324 --> 00:01:19,660
screen.

32
00:01:20,260 --> 00:01:23,267
The contact for the vendor behind a package.

33
00:01:23,267 --> 00:01:27,402
That answer sits on a second entity, reached through the first.

34
00:01:27,402 --> 00:01:28,530
Answered, and cited.

35
00:01:29,130 --> 00:01:30,606
The same six questions, asked three ways.

36
00:01:30,606 --> 00:01:31,660
The deployed site over HTTPS.

37
00:01:31,660 --> 00:01:32,925
The command line on a laptop.

38
00:01:32,925 --> 00:01:35,244
And an MCP server, started the way an editor starts one.

39
00:01:35,244 --> 00:01:37,352
One store behind all three, and the same six answers.

40
00:01:37,352 --> 00:01:39,671
The V8 graph, agents and voice frames immediately after this scene

41
00:01:39,671 --> 00:01:40,725
are silent visual proof beats.

42
00:01:40,725 --> 00:01:43,044
Their on-screen copy is generated by `build.mjs`; they are not narration

43
00:01:43,044 --> 00:01:44,730
and `narrate.mjs` must not create audio for them.

44
00:01:59,130 --> 00:02:01,609
HydraDB Cloud holds all of it.

45
00:02:01,609 --> 00:02:03,674
Seventy two conversations as evidence.

46
00:02:03,674 --> 00:02:06,153
Eighty six entity records as claims.

47
00:02:06,153 --> 00:02:10,697
Evidence and claims kept apart, because they are different kinds of

48
00:02:10,697 --> 00:02:11,110
thing.

49
00:02:11,710 --> 00:02:15,961
HydraDB builds a graph of its own from the same transcripts.

50
00:02:15,961 --> 00:02:19,439
Walked for one subject, it reaches twenty one edges.

51
00:02:19,439 --> 00:02:21,758
Ten are sentences saying nothing happened.

52
00:02:21,758 --> 00:02:23,690
Lacuna files none of them.

53
00:02:24,290 --> 00:02:28,145
Measured against five retrieval baselines over sixty four questions.

54
00:02:28,145 --> 00:02:32,858
The strongest baseline reaches sixty three, and spends eighteen hundred context

55
00:02:32,858 --> 00:02:34,571
tokens to do it.

56
00:02:34,571 --> 00:02:37,570
Lacuna answers all sixty four, on eighteen.

57
00:02:38,170 --> 00:02:42,664
The same sixty four questions asked of a self hosted node

58
00:02:42,664 --> 00:02:45,932
and of HydraDB Cloud, compared field by field.

59
00:02:45,932 --> 00:02:46,340
Identical.

60
00:02:46,940 --> 00:02:47,823
One context.

61
00:02:47,823 --> 00:02:48,705
Any agent.

62
00:02:48,705 --> 00:02:53,559
The repository, the deployment, and every artifact behind these numbers are

63
00:02:53,559 --> 00:02:54,000
public.
